WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.830
In 2022, world energy and
commodity prices surged.

2
00:00:04.830 --> 00:00:08.190
Australia sells coal, gas and iron ore.

3
00:00:08.190 --> 00:00:12.250
By 2022, each unit of
its exports bought 81

4
00:00:12.250 --> 00:00:15.350
per cent more imports than in 2015.

5
00:00:15.350 --> 00:00:17.940
Japan imports most of its energy.

6
00:00:17.940 --> 00:00:22.080
Each unit of its exports
bought about 21 per cent fewer.

7
00:00:22.080 --> 00:00:24.960
So when a country's export prices go up,

8
00:00:24.960 --> 00:00:27.390
is that good news or bad news?

9
00:00:27.390 --> 00:00:31.130
In this mission, you'll uncover why
the pattern of what countries sell,

10
00:00:31.130 --> 00:00:32.440
and who they sell to,

11
00:00:32.440 --> 00:00:36.570
keeps shifting. Then you'll follow
a country whose exports get dearer,

12
00:00:36.570 --> 00:00:39.670
and work out what happens
to the money it brings in.

13
00:00:39.670 --> 00:00:43.320
Your mission: find out when
higher export prices really

14
00:00:43.320 --> 00:00:44.930
leave a country better off.
